From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve position invariance between GX shader variants
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: native GX rasterization contract.

The original material renderer can draw identical vertices first into depth
and then with GX_EQUAL, changing TEV inputs between passes. Aurora specializes
these passes into different shaders. Request invariant vertex positions so
backend optimizations preserve consistent positions across those programs.

Position arithmetic, vertex data, depth comparisons and blend state remain
unchanged. Pipeline cache records still regenerate shader source, so their
configuration schema does not change. This supplies the native contract;
it does not by itself establish a fix for a particular transparency artifact.

--- a/lib/gx/shader.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/shader.cpp
@@ -2025,7 +2025,7 @@
 var<uniform> ubuf: Uniform;{1}
 
 struct VertexOutput {{
-    @builtin(position) pos: vec4f,{2}
+    @builtin(position) @invariant pos: vec4f,{2}
 }};
 
 @vertex
